From 33f681aa8328cbf4c4ab8396ee1a70deb36689da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:45:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 185/214] rust: bindgen: Keep the alignment of an empty
 sched_statistics

Without CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS, struct sched_statistics has no members but is
____cacheline_aligned. bindgen 0.73 emits it as an empty #[repr(C)]
struct and drops the alignment, so rustc lays out task_struct with
`stats` at 792 where C has it at 832 (arm64, 64-byte lines), and every
later field is 40 bytes early in Rust.

Rust binder reads current->mm through these bindings in
ShrinkablePageRange::new(). On the Jolla Phone it reads
pushable_tasks.node_list.next instead, an empty list head that points to
itself, and mmgrab() increments it. The second binder device a process
opens then grabs a misaligned "mm" and oopses in rust_helper_mmgrab, and
every open before that corrupts the task's pushable list. Android opens
binder and hwbinder in one process, so it never boots.

Mark the type opaque: bindgen then emits a zero-sized blob with
#[repr(align(64))]. With bindgen's layout tests compiled, the bindings
had exactly two mismatches before (sched_statistics' alignment and
task_struct::stats) and none after.
---
 rust/bindgen_parameters | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rust/bindgen_parameters b/rust/bindgen_parameters
index 5bab3cf06..2b876fdf4 100644
--- a/rust/bindgen_parameters
+++ b/rust/bindgen_parameters
@@ -26,6 +26,12 @@
 # warning. We don't need to peek into it anyway.
 --opaque-type spinlock
 
+# Without CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS, `struct sched_statistics` is an empty
+# cacheline-aligned struct. bindgen drops the alignment of an empty struct, so
+# every `task_struct` field after `stats` (mm, pid, cred, ...) sits 40 bytes
+# early on arm64. An opaque blob keeps the alignment.
+--opaque-type sched_statistics
+
 # enums that appear in indirect function calls should specify a cfi type
 --newtype-enum fwctl_rpc_scope
 --with-attribute-custom-enum=fwctl_rpc_scope='#[cfi_encoding="15fwctl_rpc_scope"]'
-- 
2.55.0

